.TH auto-change-primary-group 8

\" auto-man2man (used in generating subcommand lists) depends on this section
.SH NAME
.PP
auto-change-primary-group - Change the primary group of a user

\" Convention:
\" Underline anything that is typed verbatim - commands, etc.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.PP
.nf 
.na
auto-change-primary-group username new-group|new-gid [directory]
.ad
.fi

.SH ARGUMENTS
.nf
.na
username            Username of the user whose primary group is to change
new-group|new-gid   New group name or numeric GID
directory           Optional directory to traverse, updating files
.ad
.fi

.SH DESCRIPTION

The
.B auto-change-primary-group
command changes the primary group of "username" to "new-group"
or to the numeric GID "new-gid".

If one or more "directory" arguments are provided,
.B auto-change-primary-group
runs auto-change-group-ownership(8) on each directory to update
group ownership of relevant files under the directory.

Note: No group ownerships are updated unless at least one directory is
explicitly indicated.  This allows ownership correction, which
is time-consuming, to be done separately if desired.

.SH RETURN VALUES

0 on success, non-zero error codes otherwise.

.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
.na
auto-change-primary-group joeuser joesgroup /home/joeuser
.ad
.fi

.SH FILES
.nf
.na
/etc/passwd, /etc/group
.ad
.fi

.SH SEE ALSO

auto-admin(8)
auto-add-group(8), auto-add-to-group(8), auto-group-check(8),
auto-change-group-gid(8), auto-remove-from-group(8),
auto-change-group-ownership(8), chgrp(8)

